CCOOOORRDDIINNAATTEESS
     Coordinates are exact by construction.  A stencil is in
     quarter-grid units and a drawing in whole ones, so the con-
     version is x4 and every pin lands on a multiple of 4 - which
     is what the loader wants.

     -ssccaallee _n divides instead, for a stencil sketched n times
     oversize so its detail was drawable at all; at -ssccaallee 44 a
     drawing unit IS a quarter unit, and a hand-cut stencil's
     detail is available.

     -oorrgg _x,_y names the grid point that becomes (0,0); the
     default is the FIRST PIN, because a stencil's origin is
     where it snaps.  A sketch with no NN markers at all falls
     back to the top-left of its printable extent, and is told on
     standard error that it has no pins.

