                  pid.sym: $(STENCILS)
                            rm -f $@
                            velsym -pfx P  PUMP  pump.d  >> $@
                            velsym -pfx V  VALVE valve.d >> $@
                            velsym -pfx TK TANK  tank.d  >> $@
                            velcheck -sym $@
                  card: pid.sym ; velinfo -symsheet pid.sym | velplot -T ps -fit -

     A stencil SKETCH is an ordinary drawing: it opens in the
     editor, prints, vveellppiiccs into the manual, and takes the whole
     revision workflow (see vveellddiiffff) unchanged - so the shop's
     stencils get revision control because they ARE drawings.
     Adding a stencil is adding a line; deleting one is deleting
     a file; there is no library format to learn and no state
     anywhere but files.

     /usr/vellum/etc/library.mk is the skeleton, and
     /usr/vellum/eg/sk holds the nine sketches that build the
     stock ppiidd library - byte for byte, which is also this con-
     verter's fix point.

