     The same conversion has an interactive face.  The editor's
     MMaakkee SSyymmbbooll item (the yy key) runs this program on the
     SELECTION, and ssyymmeeddiitt grows IImmppoorrtt ddrraawwiinngg (the ii key),
     which brings a drawing into the edit buffer under exactly
     these rules - so the promote-then-touch-up workflow is one
     set of rules in one place, and a stencil made from the board
     is byte-identical to one made from a Makefile.
